# LF everywhere, on every platform. The index is already all-LF, and eol=lf pins the
# working tree too, so autocrlf never rewrites a checkout (the "LF will be replaced by
# CRLF" warning). The .sh scripts need this: sh dies on CRLF with `^M: command not found`.
# text=auto leaves detected binaries alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
